# Spying Mission before a bleed resolves, and Freak Drive after one, in the action's windows.
# zero-vtes rules-qa (checked at 1f33be5): once blocks are declined, a bleed opens a "would be
# successful" window, the acting Methuselah first, for cards like Spying Mission (24.2); every
# action has an after-resolution window, failed ones included, for cards like Freak Drive (5.8,
# 23.3). Cards are given by VEKN ID; names and images come from the content pack (LEGAL-08).
seed 13
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
seat D dave
crypt A 200510 *6 200271 *6
library A 101857 *20 100788 *20
crypt B 200452 *12
library B 101056 *40
crypt C 200771 *12
library C 100598 *40
crypt D 200051 *12
library D 100598 *40
start

# Fast-forward: Alice has Gerard Rafin and Chester DuBois ready; her hand starts with Freak Drive
# and Spying Mission.
A> transfer +6 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> transfer +7 A:uncontrolled:2
A> move A:uncontrolled:2 ready
B> transfer +4 B:uncontrolled:1
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# Gerard bleeds Bob, who doesn't block. Before it succeeds, Alice holds the impulse: she plays
# Spying Mission on Gerard. The bleed burns no pool and is unsuccessful (24.2).
A> bleed A:ready:1
B> pass
expect window would-succeed minion
expect waiting A:resolve
A> play A:hand:2 on A:ready:1
log public A attached Spying Mission to Gerard Rafin (G3)
A> resolve failure
log public The action failed
expect pool B 26
# A failed action still has its after-resolution window (23.3), Alice first.
expect window after-resolution minion

# Declaring Chester's bleed passes it: nobody else had anything to play.
A> bleed A:ready:2
expect action bleed A blocks
B> pass
# Resolving passes the would-be-successful window the same way.
A> resolve success 1 edge
expect pool B 25
log public The action succeeded

# After it, Freak Drive [for] unlocks Chester, as the action was successful (5.8), and he bleeds
# again.
expect window after-resolution minion
A> play A:hand:1
log public A played Freak Drive
A> unlock A:ready:2
A> bleed A:ready:2
B> pass
A> resolve success 1
expect pool B 24
A> pass
expect action none
